00:06:17,647 --> 00:06:23,647
In a world gone mad, being insane was just a way to fit in.

2
00:12:35,294 --> 00:12:41,294
Adam Resurrected is a drama, war film directed by Paul Schrader.

3
00:18:52,941 --> 00:18:58,941
After again attempting to commit murder, a Jewish man with a mysterious past and extraordinary intelligence,
charisma, and body control returns to an insane asylum, where he makes a startling discovery.

4
00:25:10,588 --> 00:25:16,588
Adam Stein, played by Jeff Goldblum.

5
00:31:28,235 --> 00:31:34,235
Commandat Klein, played by Willem Dafoe.

6
00:37:45,882 --> 00:37:51,882
Dr. Nathan Gross, played by Derek Jacobi.

7
00:44:03,529 --> 00:44:09,529
Gina Grey, played by Ayelet Zurer.

8
00:50:21,176 --> 00:50:27,176
Rachel Shwester, played by Hana Laslo.

9
00:56:38,823 --> 00:56:44,823
Abe Wolfowitz, played by Joachim Król.

10
01:02:56,470 --> 01:03:02,470
Adam Resurrected (other titles: Hebrew: אדם בן כלב, romanized: Adam Ben Kelev, German: Ein Leben für ein Leben: "Life for Life") is a 2008 drama
film directed by Paul Schrader and written by Noah Stollman, based on the 1969 novel of the same name by Israeli author Yoram Kaniuk.

11
01:09:14,117 --> 01:09:20,117
The Hebrew title literally translates to Adam, Son of a Dog.

12
01:15:31,764 --> 01:15:37,764
The film tells the story of a Jewish man who, before the
Holocaust, was considered Germany's greatest entertainer.

13
01:21:49,411 --> 01:21:55,411
He is forced by a concentration camp commander to live like a
dog and entertain those condemned to death.

14
01:28:07,058 --> 01:28:13,058
After the war, in the early 1960s, he is hospitalized in a psychiatric
institution for Holocaust survivors in the Judean Desert.

15
01:34:24,705 --> 01:34:30,705
The film explores themes of israel, nazi, holocaust
(shoah), campo de concentración.

16
01:40:42,352 --> 01:40:48,352
The tone is emotional.
